1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,220
Here's every part inside your PC, and what it actually does, in under a minute.

2
00:00:05,970 --> 00:00:10,287
The power supply turns wall power into clean, low-voltage power.

3
00:00:10,567 --> 00:00:14,178
The motherboard connects everything, like the roads of a city.

4
00:00:14,928 --> 00:00:16,542
The CPU is the brain.

5
00:00:16,822 --> 00:00:19,939
It runs billions of tiny instructions every second.

6
00:00:20,219 --> 00:00:25,581
The GPU is a crowd of thousands of small cores that draws every frame you see.

7
00:00:26,331 --> 00:00:28,312
Storage is long-term memory.

8
00:00:28,592 --> 00:00:30,853
It keeps your files when the power is off.

9
00:00:31,133 --> 00:00:33,151
RAM is short-term memory.

10
00:00:33,431 --> 00:00:36,403
It's fast, but it forgets everything when you shut down.

11
00:00:37,153 --> 00:00:40,537
And the coolers pull heat away so none of it slows down.

12
00:00:40,817 --> 00:00:42,836
Want to see it all working together?

13
00:00:43,116 --> 00:00:46,073
The full animated breakdown is on the channel.

